# Xcode
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/

# The Xcode project is GENERATED from Apple/project.yml by `xcodegen generate`,
# which the README has always said and the repository did not do: the project
# was committed as well as generated, and the two writers then fought over it.
# Xcode rewrites it whenever it opens one (package resolution, its own
# bookkeeping), and every file added here regenerates it — so a `git pull` was
# refused with "local changes would be overwritten" on a file nobody had
# edited. Generation is deterministic (same project.yml, byte-identical
# output), so there is nothing in here a clone cannot rebuild with one command.
Apple/gryonixNexus.xcodeproj/

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/
# The package's own lockfile, for the same reason: it holds a DIFFERENT set of
# pins depending on who resolved it last. `swift test` inside the package
# resolves the package's graph and drops Sparkle, SwiftTerm and
# swift-argument-parser; a build of the app puts them back. It pinned nothing
# for the app either way — Xcode keeps the app's resolution inside the
# generated project.
Apple/Packages/gryonixNexus/Package.resolved

# Rust
target/

# Android. Build output, daemon caches and the machine's own SDK path: all of
# it is regenerated by a sync, and Android Studio writes into these constantly
# while the project is open.
Android/.gradle/
Android/build/
Android/*/build/
Android/.kotlin/
Android/*/.kotlin/
Android/local.properties
Android/captures/
Android/.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.hprof

# IntelliJ / Android Studio. The project model is generated from Gradle on
# every open, so nothing under .idea is worth sharing — and the parts that are
# machine-specific (JDK paths, module images) break a second checkout.
.idea/
*.iml

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local working data: regenerable or machine-specific, and binaries do not
# belong in the repository.
Tools/appstore/
Tools/hostdump/
agent-src.tar.gz

# Python bytecode from the porting scripts.
__pycache__/

# The foreign VPN cores, fetched and built by Tools/build-runtimes.sh at pinned
# tags. Hundreds of megabytes of platform-specific binary that nobody can read
# a diff of, and a repository that carries them stops being able to say what is
# in its own build. The recipe and the pins ARE committed.
/Apple/Runtimes
/Android/runtimes

# The release keystore, which is the app's identity on Android: an update
# only installs over a build signed by the same key. It lives with the owner —
# see the signing block in Android/app/build.gradle.kts.
Android/keystore.properties
Android/*.jks
Android/*.keystore

# The release APK and its feed, produced by Tools/release-android.sh. The
# artefacts are uploaded to gryonix.com, not committed.
Android/release/

# Mac DMG from Tools/build-mac-dmg.sh
Apple/build/
